# Shaping Knowledge Graphs

## Introduction

This collection of Livebooks showcases the `rudof_elixir` wrapper.

It draws upon the original tutorial: [Shaping Knowledge Graphs Jupyter book](https://rudof-project.github.io/tutorials/intro.html) which introduces knowledge graph concepts using [Rudof](https://rudof-project.github.io/rudof/).

Click a chapter to open it in Livebook. Each chapter runs as its own notebook session.

## About this adaptation

Original [tutorial](https://rudof-project.github.io/tutorials/) by Jose Emilio Labra Gayo and the Rudof tutorial contributors.

The examples have been adapted to use the Elixir wrapper (see __README.md__ in repo for details).

__Note:__ 
Rudof is also available as a [command line tool](https://rudof-project.github.io/rudof/overview.html) for which the authors provide [binaries in Windows, Linux and Mac](https://github.com/rudof-project/rudof/releases). Moreover, the [rudof](https://rudof-project.github.io/) library also contains Python bindings which are [publised in pypi](https://pypi.org/project/pyrudof/). The documentation for the Python bindings is available [here](https://pyrudof.readthedocs.io/en/latest/).

